-- title:
--   Tori of a finite subgroup of SL₂(K)
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ be a field with $2 \neq 0$, let $H$ be a finite group and let $\rho\colon H \to \mathrm{SL}_2(K)$ be an injective group homomorphism. Fix $h \in H$ such that the square of the trace $\rho(h)_{00} + \rho(h)_{11}$ is not $4$. Writing $T = C_H(\{h\})$ for the centraliser of the singleton $\{h\}$, the conclusion is a conjunction of four assertions. First, for $g \in H$, $g \in T$ if and only if $\rho(g) = x\cdot 1 + y\cdot \rho(h)$ as $2 \times 2$ matrices for some $x, y \in K$. Second, every $g \in T$ with $\rho(g) \neq 1$ and $\rho(g) \neq -1$ satisfies $C_H(\{g\}) = T$ and has $(\rho(g)_{00} + \rho(g)_{11})^2 \neq 4$. Third, $|N_H(T)| \le 2\,|T|$, where the normaliser is taken of $T$ viewed as a subset of $H$. Fourth, the number of $x \in H$ with $\rho(x) \neq \pm 1$ for which there exists $s \in H$ with $C_H(\{x\}) = \{g : s^{-1} g s \in T\}$, multiplied by $|N_H(T)|$, equals $|H| \cdot (|T| - |\{x \in H : \rho(x) = 1 \text{ or } \rho(x) = -1\}|)$, the subtraction being truncated subtraction of natural numbers.
--
--   These are the standard structural facts about the "tori" of a finite subgroup of $\mathrm{SL}_2$ over a field of characteristic $\neq 2$: the centraliser of an element with $\mathrm{tr}^2 \neq 4$ is the group of units of the quadratic algebra generated by that element, it is the common centraliser of all its non-central elements, it has index at most two in its normaliser, and the count of elements whose centraliser is conjugate to it is governed by a class equation. The result feeds the analysis of Sylow subgroups and Borel orbits in [`Matrix.SpecialLinearGroup.borel_orbit_structure_of_sylow_eq_upper`](thm.html#Matrix.SpecialLinearGroup.borel_orbit_structure_of_sylow_eq_upper) and [`Matrix.SpecialLinearGroup.card_sylow_eq_card_add_one_of_finite`](thm.html#Matrix.SpecialLinearGroup.card_sylow_eq_card_add_one_of_finite).
